# Cursor Rules — ScrollTax

> Rules and context for Cursor AI. For full details, see `CLAUDE.md`.

## Project

React Native 0.84.1 (Android-only) + TypeScript app. Penalizes doomscrolling
via XRPL crypto stakes. Kotlin foreground service monitors banned app usage.

## Key Technology

- React Native 0.84.1, TypeScript, React Navigation v7 (Stack)
- XRPL (`xrpl` v4.6) — testnet by default
- Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + RLS + Edge Functions)
- `react-native-keychain` for wallet seed storage
- `react-native-dotenv` for env vars (`@env` module)

## File Layout

- Screens: `src/screens/{auth,main,onboarding}/`
- Services: `src/services/` — singleton pattern
- Theme: `src/theme/colors.ts` + `src/context/ThemeContext.tsx`
- Types: `src/types/navigation.ts`, `src/types/env.d.ts`
- Utils: `src/utils/penaltySplit.ts` (drop-safe XRP math)
- Native: `android/app/src/main/java/com/scrolltax/` (Kotlin)
- Backend: `supabase/migrations/`, `supabase/functions/`

## Rules

### MUST

- Use `const {colors} = useTheme()` for all colors
- Use integer drops for XRP math (see `penaltySplit.ts`)
- Store wallet seeds in Keychain only (`xrpl-{userId}`)
- Check `error` from all Supabase calls
- Add RLS policies to new tables
- Add new screens to `MainStackParamList` and `RootNavigator.tsx`
- Export services as singletons

### MUST NOT

- Modify `metro.config.js` polyfill/resolver config
- Change import order in `index.js`
- Use floating-point for XRP amounts
- Store seeds in AsyncStorage, Supabase, or logs
- Hardcode color values in components
- Skip error handling on service methods
